 &#x003bc;g/dL.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp-117-1309f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ehp-117-1309" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics of 397 children in Cincinnati and Rochester cohorts.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristic</th><th align="center" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cincinnati (<italic>n</italic> = 221)</th><th align="center" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Rochester (<italic>n</italic> = 176)</th><th align="center" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Combined (<italic>n</italic> = 397)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Birth weight (g)</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3,144 &#x000b1; 457</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3225.7 &#x000b1; 506</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3,180 &#x000b1; 480</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Maternal IQ</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">75.2 &#x000b1; 9.4</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">81.1 &#x000b1; 12.6</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">77.8 &#x000b1; 11.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HOME score</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.4 &#x000b1; 6.5</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">31.9 &#x000b1; 6.3</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.3 &#x000b1; 6.4</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Maternal education (grade)</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">11.2 &#x000b1; 1.4</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.2 &#x000b1; 2.0</td><td align="center" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">11.6 &#x000b1; 1.8</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign=